  "problem": {
    "id": "train-4654",
    "question": "Tom and Devin have been teaching for a total of 70 years. Devin has been teaching for 5 less than half the number of years that Tom has. How many years has Tom been teaching?",
    "gold": "50",
    "answer": "Let x be the number of years Tom has been teaching\nDevin has been teaching for (1/2)x-5 years\n70=x+((1/2)x-5)\n70=(3/2)x-5\n75=(3/2)x\nx=<<50=50>>50\nTom has been teaching for 50 years\n#### 50"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "Let's denote the number of years Tom has been teaching as \\( T \\) and the number of years Devin has been teaching as \\( D \\). According to the problem, we have two pieces of information:\n\n1. The total number of years they have been teaching is 70.\n2. Devin has been teaching for 5 less than half the number of years that Tom has.\n\nWe can express these pieces of information as the following equations:\n\\[ T + D = 70 \\]\n\\[ D = \\frac{1}{2}T - 5 \\]\n\nWe can substitute the expression for \\( D \\) from the second equation into the first equation:\n\\[ T + \\left( \\frac{1}{2}T - 5 \\right) = 70 \\]\n\nNext, we combine like terms:\n\\[ T + \\frac{1}{2}T - 5 = 70 \\]\n\\[ \\frac{3}{2}T - 5 = 70 \\]\n\nTo isolate \\( T \\), we first add 5 to both sides of the equation:\n\\[ \\frac{3}{2}T = 75 \\]\n\nThen, we multiply both sides by \\(\\frac{2}{3}\\) to solve for \\( T \\):\n\\[ T = 75 \\times \\frac{2}{3} \\]\n\\[ T = 50 \\]\n\nSo, Tom has been teaching for \\(\\boxed{50}\\) years.",
